From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:55:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 061/342] debugger: arm64 unwinding no longer crashes on the
 vector registers

ArchitectureARM64::InitRegisterRules() set "same value" rules for DWARF
registers 64-95 (v0-v31), but the unwinder's context has only as many
rules as the architecture has registers (70). RegisterRule() returned
NULL for the rest, so the Debugger crashed as soon as it unwound through
a frame with call frame information: every crash report on arm64 ended
with the Debugger itself crashing, and with debug_server set to save
reports, each crashed Debugger started another one.

Tested on the ODROID-C2 with tools/probes/crashtest.cpp (debugger() in a
BLooper's MessageReceived): a complete report with the stack trace
through libbe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kits/debugger/arch/arm64/ArchitectureARM64.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kits/debugger/arch/arm64/ArchitectureARM64.cpp b/src/kits/debugger/arch/arm64/ArchitectureARM64.cpp
index 40b6826c27..106ec26cc9 100644
--- a/src/kits/debugger/arch/arm64/ArchitectureARM64.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/debugger/arch/arm64/ArchitectureARM64.cpp
@@ -595,9 +595,13 @@ ArchitectureARM64::InitRegisterRules(CfaContext& context) const
 
 	// The base class only sets up DWARF registers below our register count;
 	// the vector registers are 64-95. GCC assumes "same value" for them, as
-	// for the others.
-	for (int32 i = 0; i < 32; i++)
-		context.RegisterRule(kDwarfV0 + i)->SetToSameValue();
+	// for the others. The unwinder's context has as many rules as we have
+	// registers (70), so the upper vector registers have none: their CFI
+	// instructions are skipped (callee-saved d8-d15 are 72-79).
+	for (int32 i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
+		if (CfaRule* rule = context.RegisterRule(kDwarfV0 + i))
+			rule->SetToSameValue();
+	}
 
 	return B_OK;
 }
